## Tokyo 東京

It had always been my childhood dream to go to Japan. My parents would always tease or hint at bringing me one day. Even after all these years, I've still wanted to go there so much. When the plane pulled just into sight of the Tokyo coastline I looked out of the window and at the sunrise. The rising sun of the Japanese flag was so much more breath taking than I had ever imagined. Photos do not do this view justice. (And definately not the one I took below haha)

{% image src="/images/blog/japan-2018/IMG_6086.JPG" alt="Tokyo sunrise from the plane" width="full" /%}

{% photoRow images=[{src: "/images/blog/japan-2018/IMG_6113-min.JPG", alt: "Tokyo"}, {src: "/images/blog/japan-2018/IMG_6104-min.JPG", alt: "Tokyo"}] /%}

{% image src="/images/blog/japan-2018/IMG_6135-min.JPG" alt="Tokyo" width="full" /%}

My first two meals were these two delicious ramen dishes. About 400 and 600 yen respectively. ($5.00 & $8.00)

{% photoRow images=[{src: "/images/blog/japan-2018/IMG_6117-min.JPG", alt: "Ramen dish"}, {src: "/images/blog/japan-2018/IMG_6126-min.JPG", alt: "Ramen dish"}] /%}

Tokyo was just where I met up with my parents flying in from overseas. We went straight to Osaka the next day.

## Osaka 大阪市

Osaka was just an unreal blend of city night life fantastic eateries and traditional architecture. We spent a good 3 days here.

